{
  "schema": 1,
  "data": "benchmarks.cells:carry_cell",
  "note": "THE CARRY FAMILY'S CELLS, AS DATA. One record per cell; tests and the benches read this file instead of each keeping their own copy. A record is a DECLARATION of a draw and a shape, never of an arm: the arm key is (D, DV, warps_per_cta) and is derived from `widths`, `dv` and `warps_per_cta` by rola.ops.carry.",
  "fields": {
    "name": "the cell's identity; a seed is derived from it (crc32) so a failure reproduces from its own name",
    "widths": "the descriptor's PADDED per-level digit counts B_l (powers of two at or above 16)",
    "dv": "the descriptor's PADDED value width DV, one of rola.ops.carry.SHIPPED_DV",
    "tokens": "L, the sequence length in tokens; any L is lawful (the kernel runs a partial window)",
    "warps_per_cta": "the launch shape; 8 is shipped, 4 is the two-CTA latency diagnostic",
    "draw": "dense | alt | both | cohort | dead | deposit | tied | anti | cold | readonly | concentrated | onehot | flip -- which support structure the routing is drawn with (benchmarks.cells.realize and _corner); `dead` puts zero amplitude everywhere and `deposit` makes exactly one token write exactly one leaf",
    "k_tok": "nonzeros per row per sparse level; a property of the DRAW and never told to the kernel",
    "cohort": "for draw=cohort, the run of consecutive tokens sharing one contiguous digit window",
    "support": "the leading fraction of each level's digits the draw may use (structured truncation); for draw=cold, the fraction of level zero's digits the WRITE side may use",
    "backing": "dense | paged -- which state backing the cell binds",
    "state": "none | fresh | carried -- whether the cell binds an entry state and chains; a carried cell's entry state is drawn with it (RealizedCell.entry)",
    "tier": "oracle | probe | both -- who reads this record. The `one-box-*` cells are the SANITIZER LANE's declared shape: N = BC, so the launch is one CTA and racecheck sees the whole of the shared memory the design has, at 1/256 the record memory of a flagship cell",
    "regime": "where the draw sits on every axis of benchmarks.cells.regimes.REGIME_AXES; realize proves it and refuses a draw that is elsewhere. null for dead and deposit, which state their support themselves"
  },
